he left and the constant on the right:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3x + y &= -1 \\\\\n-6x - 3y &= 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we multiply the first equation by $-2$, then we will get a $6x$ term that can cancel with the $-6x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\{-3x + y = -1 \\mid \\mid \\cdot (-2); -6x - 3y = 8\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, the $x$ terms cancel, and we can solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x - 2y &= 2 \\\\\n-6x - 3y &= 8 \\\\\n-5y &= (2 + 8) \\\\\n-5y &= 10 \\\\\ny &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3x + (1)(-2) &= -1 \\\\\n-3x &= 1 \\\\\nx &= - \\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system has *a single solution*, $(- \\frac{1}{3},-2)$." 13194139535799 17592186045443 true] [17592186529285 1080 "no solutions" 13194139535799 17592186045443 true] [17592186529285 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535799 17592186045443 true] [17592186529285 1083 #uuid "71a19f9f-c97f-5b22-a3fb-3ddd84649033" 13194139535799 17592186045443 true] [17592186529286 1080 "infinitely many solutions" 13194139535799 17592186045443 true] [17592186529286 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535799 17592186045443 true] [17592186529286 1083 #uuid "72bba841-9529-5598-b921-f90b8dffbe5b" 13194139535799 17592186045443 true] [17592186529287 1075 #edb/ref 17592186529276 13194139535799 17592186045443 true] [17592186529287 1075 #edb/ref 17592186529299 13194139535799 17592186045443 true] [17592186529287 1075 #edb/ref 17592186529305 13194139535799 17592186045443 true] [17592186529287 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139535799 17592186045443 true] [17592186529287 1077 "field-1" 13194139535799 17592186045443 true] [17592186529287 1078 #edb/ref 17592186529305 13194139535799 17592186045443 true] [17592186529287 1079 #uuid "766ff9b6-bfc6-59ad-af1f-7918abd24f91" 13194139535799 17592186045443 true] [17592186529288 1080 "a single solution" 13194139535799 17592186045443 true] [17592186529288 1082 #edb/ref 175